    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n89611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσ-κλῐσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leaning against</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῴου πρὸς δένδρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					3.27
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>genuflexion</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Myst.</u>
				1.12
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>inclination, predilection</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν γερόντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					6.10.10
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> to one, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.51.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἵρεσίς ἐστι π. δογμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Stoic.</u>
					2.37
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. δόγμασιν</span> ibid., <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				<u>Prooem.</u>
				20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ -κλίσεως</span> Carnead.
			and Clitomach. ap. eund.ib.<i><span class="en">
				230
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ πρόσκλισιν</span> with
				<i>partiality</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Ti.</u>
				5.21
			</span></i>.</div>
